{title: Harbor Bells}
{artist: The Tidewater Few}
{capo: 4}
{tempo: 96}

{comment: Tuning: Standard (E A D G B E)}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[C]Harbor bells are [G]ringing out the hour
[Am]Fishermen are men[F]ding in the shower
[C]Gulls are arguing [G]about the bread
[Am]Somebody's sin[F]ging in the [C]shed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Ring, ring, h[C]arbor bells
[G]Every sailor kno[Am]ws the spell
[F]Ring, ring, h[C]arbor bells
[G]Bring them home a[C]nd all is well
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[C]Lighthouse keeper c[G]ounting every mast
[Am]Writing down the [F]ones that sail past
[C]Tides are turning [G]like a page
[Am]Every wave a lit[F]tle older th[C]an its age
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Ring, ring, h[C]arbor bells
[G]Every sailor kno[Am]ws the spell
[F]Ring, ring, h[C]arbor bells
[G]Bring them home a[C]nd all is well
{end_of_chorus}
